        "id": "b1",
        "chapter_id": "ch1",
        "text": "Mira Thorn began her service as a young apprentice. At that time her speaking voice was light, and she spoke quietly when practicing her announcements alone.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch1.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b1",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b2",
        "chapter_id": "ch2",
        "text": "Twenty years later Captain Thorn entered the same shipyard. Captain Thorn was Mira Thorn herself, the former apprentice, now promoted. The title did not belong to another person.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch2.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b2",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b3",
        "chapter_id": "ch2",
        "text": "An old throat injury had made Mira's voice rougher and lower. She practiced firm commands as captain, then tried the same words in a softer tone. Her age, rank, injury, and changing manner of speech did not turn her into a different person.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch2.xhtml",
